# <type>(<scope>): <short imperative summary>
#
# Why:
# Explain the problem, context, or user need behind this change.
#
# What changed:
# - Summarize the important implementation details.
# - Call out architectural, deployment, or dependency changes.
# - Note any content or behavior that was intentionally preserved.
#
# Verification:
# - List the checks actually run, including build, lint, typecheck,
#   browser verification, and Lighthouse results where applicable.
#
# Refs: #
#
# Conventional commit types:
# feat, fix, refactor, perf, docs, build, ci, test, chore
#
# Subject rules:
# - Use imperative mood: "add", "fix", "migrate", not "added" or "adds".
# - Keep the first line at or below 72 characters.
# - Do not end the subject with a period.
#
# Body rules:
# - Separate the subject from the body with one blank line.
# - Wrap the body at 72 characters.
# - Use the footer for issue references or breaking changes.
#
# Breaking change format:
# BREAKING CHANGE: describe the migration or compatibility impact.
